142	// reclassifyFacts backfills the deterministic derived fields — KIND and LOCUS —
143	// onto facts in place and returns the count of facts changed. KIND is filled
144	// only when missing/invalid (force recomputes it, e.g. after the inference rules
145	// change); LOCUS is purely a function of the text, so it is always reconciled to
146	// the computed set. It deliberately does NOT bump UpdatedAt — these are additive
147	// metadata, not a content edit, so the backfill stays invisible to recency
