11	// Backlog UX-21. About a hundred remedies hardcoded `entire brain <verb>`. On a
12	// plugin-style install the runnable spelling is the binary's own name, so each of
13	// them told the reader to type a command that does not exist for them. The
14	// guards below hold the fix from two directions: no source line may print the
15	// hardcoded spelling again (static, with a floor so it cannot match nothing),
16	// and the remedies that were converted must render in the spelling the
17	// environment dictates, in both modes (behavioural).
